{"shortDescription":"Asia's naphtha prices rose on Thursday, in line with crude oil benchmarks, as supplies from the Middle East remained scarce, traders said.The price for first-half November cargo rose by $11.50 to about $927 per metric ton. The crack for naphtha declined to about $131 per ton over Brent crude.In the…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Asia's naphtha prices rose on Thursday, in line with crude oil benchmarks, as supplies from the Middle East remained scarce, traders said."]},{"type":"p","children":["The price for first-half November cargo rose by $11.50 to about $927 per metric ton. The crack for naphtha declined to about $131 per ton over Brent crude."]},{"type":"p","children":["In the gasoline market, the crack remained firm at around $37 per barrel over Brent crude amid strong demand and tight supplies."]},{"type":"p","children":["Asia's largest buyer Indonesia sought more gasoline of 90-octane grade and benchmark grade for November delivery, market participants said. They sought several cargoes earlier this month for October delivery."]},{"type":"p","children":["INVENTORIES"]},{"type":"p","children":["Light distillates stocks, including naphtha and gasoline, fell to a three-week low of 11.78 million barrels in the week to September 23, Enterprise Singapore data showed."]},{"type":"p","children":["Naphtha imports stood at about 268,000 tons (approximately 2.4 million barrels), led by Russia at nearly 148,000 tons, followed by Kuwait at around 29,000 tons."]},{"type":"p","children":["Singapore exported about 17,000 tons of naphtha, with all shipments destined for Indonesia."]},{"type":"p","children":["NEWS"]},{"type":"p","children":["- Oil prices rose more than 2% on Thursday as diplomatic talks between the US and Iran showed little sign of progress, while investors focused on uncertainty about a potential US ban on diesel exports."]},{"type":"p","children":["- China's gasoline and diesel inventories have falle